issues.body:
We currently define a special rule to convey a public device binding key. Could we generalize this and allow claims to point to an array of messages instead of a single message? Something like this:

```json
{
  "alg": "BBS-MOD",
  "vct": "https://credentials.example.com/identity_credential",
  "cmap": {
    "given_name": [0, false],
    "family_name": [1, false],
    "email": [2, false],
    "phone_number": [3, false],
    "address": {
      "street_address": [4, false],
      "locality": [5, false],
      "region": [6, false],
      "country": [7, false]
    },
    "birthdate": [8, true],
    "iat": [9, true],
    "exp": [10, true]
    "cnf": {
      "bls12-381": [[11,12,13,14], true]
    }
  }
}
```

This contains a (simplified) cnf claim that conveys the public key (4 limbs, 2 per x/y value) of the device binding key.  This would allow us to remove any special parsing rules for the `kb` header fields and make the mechanism more future-proof. If the scalar raw encoding goes into the blind bbs signature draft, it would become especially nice (removing the boolean flag for our data structure) - see #5 :

```json
{
  "alg": "BBS-MOD",
  "vct": "https://credentials.example.com/identity_credential",
  "cmap": {
    "given_name": [0],
    "family_name": [1],
    "email": [2],
    "phone_number": [3],
    "address": {
      "street_address": [4],
      "locality": [5],
      "region": [6],
      "country": [7]
    },
    "birthdate": [8],
    "iat": [9],
    "exp": [10]
    "cnf": {
      "bls12-381": [11,12,13,14]
    }
  }
}
```
